      "id": "weekend-2026-10-17",
      "date": "2026-10-17T07:00:00+04:00",
      "title": "Weekend wrap: AI jitters, hot inflation and $100 oil",
      "bias": "neutral",
      "markets": ["gold", "silver", "oil", "eurusd", "usdjpy", "spx", "nasdaq", "nifty", "btc", "dfm"],
      "points": [
        "Hot September US inflation (3.7%) revived Fed hike talk and lifted yields; markets still mostly expect a hold on 28 Oct.",
        "US stocks fell on Friday as AI spending and debt worries hit tech: the S&P 500 lost 1.1% to 7,659 and the Nasdaq 2.1% to 26,140. Energy was the only strong sector.",
        "Oil stays firm on Middle East supply risk: Brent traded above $106 and WTI near $96, with $100 the next test.",
        "Gold recovered from its post-CPI drop to about $4,166 but remains boxed between $4,100 and $4,200. Silver is weaker, near $57 and close to oversold.",
        "The dollar had its first weekly fall in five weeks, yet EUR/USD is still capped by its downtrend line near 1.1250 and USD/JPY sits around 158.",
        "India stood out: Nifty rose 0.65% to 23,146 and broke a six-week losing streak.",
        "Bitcoin held around $81,000–82,500 despite the inflation data, but stays below its $84,200 breakout level. Dubai stocks drifted near a six-week low.",
        "Week ahead: Big Tech earnings, Fed speakers into the 27–28 Oct meeting, and oil headlines from the Middle East."
